      },
      "lineNbr": 86,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:08:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It will be repeated I/O - the same I/O cost, whether it happens in a single  ReadFullyAtOffset call or another.\n\nStill, it would be better to re-use the buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "3ca80d90_34b019f5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 86,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 86,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "d2a001a4762d18144ec6c9a743c3d26bb77b9638",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61f06cd8_6a93c695",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_content_FileSystemUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 86,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:14:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So:\n1. move the buffer outside of the loop\n2. prefer malloc/realloc instead of using std::vector, so if this returns nullptr, you can return, instead of aborting on out of memory\n3. please do chunking if you can, it could be like this, maybe?\n\n```\nconstexpr size_t kChunk \u003d 60 * 1024;\nfor (size_t i \u003d punchLen; i \u003c punchStartOffset; i +\u003d kChunk) {\n    size_t uncheckedChunkEnd;\n    if (!__builtin_add_overflow(i, kChunk, \u0026uncheckedChunkEnd)) ...\n    ... \u003d ReadFullyAtOffset(fd, buffer.data(), i, std::min(uncheckedChunkEnd, punchStartOffset));\n    ...\n    fallocate\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a778ce5f_6145899c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 86,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 86,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "d2a001a4762d18144ec6c9a743c3d26bb77b9638",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e65d231_f7bb25d3",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_content_FileSystemUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 86,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:18:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also if you use chunking, you don\u0027t need realloc, and you can use:\n\n```\nconstexpr size_t kChunk \u003d 60 * 1024;\nuint8_t* buffer \u003d (uint8_t*)malloc(kChunk);\nif (buffer \u003d\u003d nullptr) return ...; // (OOM)\n\nfor (size_t index \u003d 0; programHeaders.size() \u003e\u003d 2 ... {\n    ...\n    for ... { // iterate over chunks\n        ReadFullyAtOffset..\n        fallocate...\n    }\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "61f06cd8_6a93c695",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 86,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 86,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "d2a001a4762d18144ec6c9a743c3d26bb77b9638",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
