      },
      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T23:41:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "memcmp is a compiler builtin and it does realize what\u0027s going on here (compares to 0), but yeah I actually can\u0027t believe how much the the lambda is optimized for this case (it\u0027s unrolled - and memcpy doesn\u0027t get unrolled here) - I guess I\u0027m used to seeing bigger lambdas?\n\nAnyway, we could do the test, but I std::all_of does seem faster to me for -Os, which we use in Android:\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/zeedeo1eY\n\nThanks Kelvin!",
      "parentUuid": "f1ef50b9_0896de15",
